1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,399
(Previously)
We must hurry and take action.

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,800
We don't know when the two captured men
will spill the beans.

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:09,100
No matter what happens, please know, Your
Highness, that I have never meant you any harm.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,800
Hey! Seize Prince Thin!
You are the honor of this royal family!

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,700
If having honor means living without
Phob... I would rather have nothing at all!

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,000
Thin!

7
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,999
Grandma is giving this to you.
Take it to start over,

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,500
go and be with the one you love.

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,700
Khana Ratsadon has now successfully
seized control of the government.

10
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:04,000
"The Edge of Horizon"
(Episode 8)

11
00:02:04,262 --> 00:02:05,263
[Noppalak Palace]

12
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:15,701
You traitorous rebel!

13
00:02:17,174 --> 00:02:19,014
How dare you go against
the Crown's authority?

14
00:02:20,228 --> 00:02:22,582
You are leading Siam to its destruction!

15
00:02:25,956 --> 00:02:27,982
We're creating a new Siam.

16
00:02:29,788 --> 00:02:31,022
The old system has failed.

17
00:02:32,332 --> 00:02:34,102
It's holding our country back.

18
00:02:36,390 --> 00:02:39,022
This land belongs to the people.

19
00:02:40,222 --> 00:02:41,982
Everyone deserves equal rights.

20
00:02:44,556 --> 00:02:46,142
Equal rights?

21
00:02:48,652 --> 00:02:49,653
You really believe that?

22
00:02:50,665 --> 00:02:54,222
Do you think those fancy ideals
can actually build a nation?

23
00:02:54,862 --> 00:02:55,863
At least,

24
00:02:57,182 --> 00:02:59,142
it gives hope to people who've got nothing.

25
00:03:00,081 --> 00:03:03,862
So you think destroying everything
we've built is the answer?

26
00:03:06,793 --> 00:03:07,862
If what we have now

27
00:03:09,476 --> 00:03:11,382
keeps most people at the bottom,

28
00:03:12,014 --> 00:03:13,622
then it deserves to be changed.

29
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,022
We're doing this for our country.

30
00:03:18,078 --> 00:03:19,542
For our country?

31
00:03:20,516 --> 00:03:23,036
You've got some nerve saying that
after everything you've done.

32
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:28,020
I'm doing this for the greater good.

33
00:03:29,273 --> 00:03:30,382
I haven't betrayed anyone.

34
00:03:32,228 --> 00:03:34,142
You betrayed me!

35
00:03:35,753 --> 00:03:39,222
I raised you and paid for your education.

36
00:03:39,942 --> 00:03:42,782
And now you stand here,
acting all superior to me?

37
00:03:48,561 --> 00:03:49,562
An education?

38
00:03:51,206 --> 00:03:52,710
Just so I can serve the royals?

39
00:03:55,953 --> 00:03:59,540
They only want smart
servants to do their bidding.

40
00:04:00,857 --> 00:04:03,844
So that's how you've felt all this time

41
00:04:04,724 --> 00:04:06,742
while you were living
at Varakulvatin Palace?

42
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:20,961
I'll always be grateful to the palace.

43
00:04:22,934 --> 00:04:24,374
But I have to stand with the people.

44
00:04:26,214 --> 00:04:27,942
How admirable.

45
00:04:29,516 --> 00:04:31,382
Captain Phobthee will do anything

46
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:34,342
to achieve your goal.

47
00:04:36,076 --> 00:04:39,142
Even getting close to Tinnakorn again
was part of your plan, wasn't it?

48
00:04:39,297 --> 00:04:40,622
I truly love Prince Tinnakorn.

49
00:04:41,610 --> 00:04:44,342
Someone as wicked as you
actually knows what love is?

50
00:04:49,814 --> 00:04:52,022
You never saw me as your equal.

51
00:04:54,732 --> 00:04:57,892
You never believed my love was real,
because I was nothing more than a servant.

52
00:04:58,022 --> 00:05:00,742
But this lowly servant will prove

53
00:05:00,892 --> 00:05:02,462
that everyone deserves equal rights,

54
00:05:02,625 --> 00:05:04,826
dignity, and the right to love.

55
00:05:05,393 --> 00:05:09,462
Love is for those who
are honest and sincere,

56
00:05:09,932 --> 00:05:12,502
not for someone who's
willing to use it as a weapon.

57
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:19,422
I stand by my words.

58
00:05:21,323 --> 00:05:22,942
I truly love Prince Tinnakorn.

59
00:05:25,377 --> 00:05:26,378
Are you sure?

60
00:05:28,369 --> 00:05:31,902
Are you sure you never used Tinnakorn
for your political agenda?

61
00:05:35,329 --> 00:05:37,617
No matter how much you change the world,

62
00:05:38,198 --> 00:05:40,142
and make everyone equal,

63
00:05:40,922 --> 00:05:43,302
you'll never be worthy of him.

64
00:06:09,564 --> 00:06:10,565
Oy!

65
00:06:12,822 --> 00:06:15,102
- Can you give this back to Grandma?
- Yes, Your Highness.

66
00:06:19,084 --> 00:06:20,161
Let me go!

67
00:06:20,682 --> 00:06:23,862
You traitors! I will kill you all!

68
00:06:24,182 --> 00:06:26,183
- Chat! Hey!
- Tin! Help me!

69
00:06:26,193 --> 00:06:28,262
- Chat!
- Your Highness!

70
00:06:28,412 --> 00:06:29,702
Please, don't follow him.

71
00:06:29,772 --> 00:06:31,102
I need to help my brother.

72
00:06:31,462 --> 00:06:33,542
We don't know who we can trust right now.

73
00:06:34,238 --> 00:06:36,582
I'm afraid they might take you as well.

74
00:06:37,542 --> 00:06:39,022
How is everyone?

75
00:06:39,484 --> 00:06:41,622
Your grandma and the rest of us are safe.

76
00:06:42,156 --> 00:06:46,462
But we didn't hear
anything from your father.

77
00:06:47,318 --> 00:06:48,319
Dad?

78
00:06:51,137 --> 00:06:54,038
Why didn't you run away with Phob?

79
00:06:54,470 --> 00:06:56,750
I didn't even get to see Phob
before everything happened.

80
00:06:58,897 --> 00:06:59,898
I totally forgot.

81
00:07:01,905 --> 00:07:02,906
Phob is a soldier.

82
00:07:04,129 --> 00:07:06,782
I will ask him to help us.

83
00:07:07,489 --> 00:07:09,222
- Okay.
- I need to find him.

84
00:07:09,345 --> 00:07:10,622
Please be careful.

85
00:07:15,121 --> 00:07:17,742
HTMS Sukhothai should arrive
in Hua Hin tomorrow morning.

86
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:20,692
Once His Majesty

87
00:07:22,249 --> 00:07:24,382
receives the petition
inviting him to return,

88
00:07:25,764 --> 00:07:28,473
we'll know whether the
country will remain peaceful...

89
00:07:30,062 --> 00:07:31,302
or be plunged into bloodshed.

90
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:43,382
We've reinforced all the strategic
positions around the capital.

91
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:49,262
If the provincial troops
try to march back in,

92
00:07:52,329 --> 00:07:54,022
they'll have to get past our guns first.

93
00:07:57,337 --> 00:08:00,662
Keep the members of the royal family
in custody. No disturbances

94
00:08:01,497 --> 00:08:03,502
until we receive word from Hua Hin.

95
00:08:04,468 --> 00:08:05,469
Yes, sir.

96
00:08:28,582 --> 00:08:31,583
I heard you went to talk to
Prince Vasin, how did it go?

97
00:08:33,110 --> 00:08:34,111
What do you think?

98
00:08:36,417 --> 00:08:37,862
He was furious at us,

99
00:08:39,070 --> 00:08:40,271
he called us rebels.

100
00:08:42,809 --> 00:08:43,942
He also accused me of

101
00:08:45,364 --> 00:08:46,822
using Prince Tinnakorn.

102
00:08:50,468 --> 00:08:53,942
Prince Tinnakorn is staying
at the house you rented, isn't he?

103
00:08:57,444 --> 00:09:00,902
Once this is over, you
have to explain it to him.

104
00:09:01,252 --> 00:09:03,332
Make him understand that
we did this for the people.

105
00:09:11,129 --> 00:09:13,222
I just hope Prince
Tinnakorn will understand.

106
00:09:33,438 --> 00:09:35,470
Phob! You're back.

107
00:09:36,356 --> 00:09:37,622
Are you okay, honey?

108
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:39,742
I'm fine, Mom.

109
00:09:41,487 --> 00:09:43,542
The whole city is in chaos.

110
00:09:43,964 --> 00:09:47,462
They say the rebels have
rounded up all the royals.

111
00:09:47,814 --> 00:09:49,654
I was so afraid something
might happen to you.

112
00:09:51,038 --> 00:09:52,522
I wonder

113
00:09:52,942 --> 00:09:55,726
how everyone at Varakulvatin
Palace is holding up.

114
00:09:58,420 --> 00:10:01,622
It's alright, Mom. The
soldiers are taking care of them.

115
00:10:03,622 --> 00:10:04,623
Taking care of?

116
00:10:05,623 --> 00:10:06,624
How?

117
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:11,722
Keeping an eye on them.

118
00:10:14,001 --> 00:10:15,841
The soldiers are there
to prevent any trouble.

119
00:10:18,444 --> 00:10:21,777
As for Prince Wasin, he's currently
being held at Noppalak Palace.

120
00:10:23,068 --> 00:10:24,869
If the situation remains peaceful

121
00:10:25,244 --> 00:10:27,222
and the royals accept
the change in government,

122
00:10:27,414 --> 00:10:28,742
we'll release him.

123
00:10:33,233 --> 00:10:34,234
We?

124
00:10:36,054 --> 00:10:37,055
You mean…

125
00:10:40,396 --> 00:10:41,397
you…

126
00:10:44,870 --> 00:10:46,142
you are a rebel?

127
00:10:48,041 --> 00:10:49,062
It's not like that.

128
00:10:50,042 --> 00:10:52,582
Rebels are those who betray their country

129
00:10:52,622 --> 00:10:53,758
for personal power.

130
00:10:54,522 --> 00:10:56,662
We're fighting for the power of the people.

131
00:11:01,089 --> 00:11:04,272
By betraying the people who took you in?

132
00:11:10,708 --> 00:11:13,241
How could you do this?

133
00:11:15,097 --> 00:11:17,382
Even a dog knows better.

134
00:11:18,382 --> 00:11:22,042
It would never bite the hand that feeds it.

135
00:11:24,430 --> 00:11:26,122
We are not dogs.

136
00:11:26,969 --> 00:11:29,689
We don't have to be grateful for
whatever scraps they throw our way.

137
00:11:34,708 --> 00:11:37,462
We're all human, including the royals.

138
00:11:38,313 --> 00:11:40,636
We deserve the same dignity and respect.

139
00:11:41,713 --> 00:11:43,672
We shouldn't have to bow to them forever.

140
00:11:48,113 --> 00:11:49,114
At first,

141
00:11:50,241 --> 00:11:52,822
when you went back to Prince Tinnakorn,

142
00:11:55,422 --> 00:11:59,796
I thought it was because you still loved
him... that you could never let him go.

143
00:12:01,577 --> 00:12:06,022
But was this the real reason
you went back to him?

144
00:12:12,609 --> 00:12:14,722
I did what I had to do.

145
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:14,022
Phob, have you heard the rumors

146
00:13:14,982 --> 00:13:17,022
about a plot to overthrow the government?

147
00:13:18,502 --> 00:13:20,022
Yes, I've heard about it.

148
00:13:21,007 --> 00:13:23,422
Stay away from those people.

149
00:13:25,185 --> 00:13:26,985
My dad used to suspect
you to be one of them.

150
00:13:27,806 --> 00:13:29,262
I don't want you to be in danger.

151
00:13:41,422 --> 00:13:42,423
P.T.

152
00:13:44,758 --> 00:13:45,759
Phobthee.

153
00:13:47,302 --> 00:13:48,303
Tinnakorn.

154
00:13:52,273 --> 00:13:54,122
Phob, do you like it?

155
00:13:55,745 --> 00:13:58,022
I asked them to make it special for us.

156
00:13:59,156 --> 00:14:00,157
Of course, I do.

157
00:14:00,382 --> 00:14:01,383
Phob! Oh!

158
00:14:06,116 --> 00:14:07,117
Put me down.

159
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:11,522
Why? Why, Phob? Why!

160
00:14:17,014 --> 00:14:18,015
Why?

161
00:14:36,046 --> 00:14:37,522
Why?

162
00:14:52,390 --> 00:14:54,897
Who's that? Who is sitting here?

163
00:14:56,097 --> 00:14:58,396
What? Tinnakorn?

164
00:14:58,708 --> 00:15:01,582
What is going on? Why are you sitting here?

165
00:15:01,718 --> 00:15:03,622
I thought you went to see Phob.

166
00:15:06,502 --> 00:15:07,503
Darling?

167
00:15:08,718 --> 00:15:09,719
What's wrong?

168
00:15:11,362 --> 00:15:13,363
Tinnakorn? Aum, faster!

169
00:15:13,407 --> 00:15:15,760
[June 25, 1932]

170
00:15:20,540 --> 00:15:22,166
I hope they choose to surrender.

171
00:15:22,849 --> 00:15:24,822
I don't want this to
escalate into a civil war.

172
00:15:31,172 --> 00:15:32,522
Any news from Hua Hin, sir?

173
00:15:33,118 --> 00:15:34,372
What did the royals say?

174
00:15:37,801 --> 00:15:38,802
His Majesty

175
00:15:39,830 --> 00:15:43,062
will grant us the
constitution we've requested.

176
00:15:47,472 --> 00:15:49,822
Come on, everyone!
The revolution has begun!

177
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:57,142
We did it, Phob! Siam is going to change!

178
00:16:04,452 --> 00:16:06,452
You're worried about
Prince Tinnakorn, aren't you?

179
00:16:12,598 --> 00:16:14,522
I will explain to him and
make him understand.

180
00:16:24,694 --> 00:16:27,645
His Majesty issued a
royal letter in response to

181
00:16:27,670 --> 00:16:32,342
the Khana Ratsadon's Military Committee
for the Defense of the Capital, stating:

182
00:16:32,652 --> 00:16:36,182
"For the sake of peace and
order among my people,"

183
00:16:36,348 --> 00:16:38,022
"I do not wish to see any bloodshed."

184
00:16:38,102 --> 00:16:41,093
"In truth, I had already been considering"

185
00:16:41,103 --> 00:16:43,104
"a change along these very lines."

186
00:16:43,142 --> 00:16:45,262
"I therefore agree to
serve as a figurehead,"

187
00:16:45,272 --> 00:16:48,534
"so that the establishment
of the new government"

188
00:16:48,609 --> 00:16:51,542
"and the adoption of a
constitution may proceed smoothly."

189
00:16:51,676 --> 00:16:54,822
"For if I were to refuse this role,"

190
00:16:54,996 --> 00:16:57,852
"foreign nations would likely
refuse to recognize the new government."

191
00:17:05,948 --> 00:17:07,522
What does it mean, Your Highness?

192
00:17:17,022 --> 00:17:19,722
His Majesty didn't want to see
the people shed each other's blood.

193
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:22,823
And to keep the country moving forward

194
00:17:24,134 --> 00:17:26,462
without any more turmoil,

195
00:17:28,561 --> 00:17:30,761
he agreed to the change in
Siam's system of government.

196
00:17:44,116 --> 00:17:46,436
The King didn't want to see
the country thrown into chaos,

197
00:17:46,910 --> 00:17:49,382
so he agreed to the
Khana Ratsadon's requests.

198
00:17:53,750 --> 00:17:54,751
No! No!

199
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:56,301
This is not true!

200
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:00,413
No! No!

201
00:18:07,278 --> 00:18:10,089
Listen up, everyone. Gather around!

202
00:18:10,532 --> 00:18:12,222
The King has agreed!

203
00:18:12,825 --> 00:18:16,890
As His Majesty King Prajadhipok

204
00:18:16,915 --> 00:18:26,163
has signed the Temporary Constitution
of the Kingdom of Siam, B.E. 2475 (1932),

205
00:18:26,576 --> 00:18:30,976
From this day forward, supreme authority
shall reside in the People's Assembly.

206
00:18:31,363 --> 00:18:34,751
The affairs of state shall be
administered under the supervision

207
00:18:34,775 --> 00:18:37,481
of its executive body, known as
the People's Committee of Siam.

208
00:18:37,746 --> 00:18:41,883
To exercise supervision over
the administration of nation affairs

209
00:18:57,425 --> 00:18:59,662
It is over now, Your Highness.

210
00:19:07,958 --> 00:19:09,342
Everything has proceeded peacefully.

211
00:19:11,473 --> 00:19:12,742
We are not rebels.

212
00:19:15,332 --> 00:19:17,122
We are carrying out His Majesty's wishes,

213
00:19:18,361 --> 00:19:21,342
wishes he accepted to spare
the nation from bloodshed.

214
00:19:28,001 --> 00:19:29,862
You wretched traitors!

215
00:19:31,004 --> 00:19:32,724
You forced His Majesty into agreeing to it.

216
00:19:36,430 --> 00:19:38,550
His Majesty has acted in
the nation's best interests.

217
00:19:40,622 --> 00:19:42,502
You should respect His Majesty's wishes and

218
00:19:44,644 --> 00:19:46,222
not bring about any further unrest.

219
00:19:48,708 --> 00:19:52,122
From this day on, Siam
belongs to all its people,

220
00:19:56,310 --> 00:19:57,542
not only the aristocracy.

221
00:20:00,652 --> 00:20:03,142
Don't think it'll be that easy.

222
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:06,662
As long as I'm alive,

223
00:20:07,524 --> 00:20:09,302
you'll never get what you want.

224
00:20:10,521 --> 00:20:12,622
I'll never surrender to the likes of you.

225
00:20:16,036 --> 00:20:17,322
As for Tinnakorn,

226
00:20:18,665 --> 00:20:20,582
I am certain he will not forgive you.

227
00:20:29,118 --> 00:20:30,742
I'll escort you back to the palace.

228
00:20:35,119 --> 00:20:36,120
This way, please.

229
00:20:57,881 --> 00:21:00,172
How is Tinnakorn?

230
00:21:00,596 --> 00:21:03,022
The prince is up but
he still looks exhausted.

231
00:21:04,089 --> 00:21:06,262
What was going on with him?

232
00:21:06,316 --> 00:21:07,902
I thought he went to see Phob,

233
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:09,782
but where is Phob?

234
00:21:10,069 --> 00:21:14,295
Vasin and Chatthorn
haven't been home either.

235
00:21:14,497 --> 00:21:17,622
Aum, I'm starting to get
worried. What should I do?

236
00:21:19,014 --> 00:21:20,222
Chat, darling?

237
00:21:20,705 --> 00:21:22,422
How are you?

238
00:21:23,713 --> 00:21:25,982
Have a seat next to me. How are you doing?

239
00:21:27,022 --> 00:21:30,622
I'm fine. They kept me in jail

240
00:21:30,822 --> 00:21:31,862
and they just released me.

241
00:21:32,722 --> 00:21:35,082
May you be blessed,
and may Heaven watch over you, darling.

242
00:21:39,676 --> 00:21:41,582
Prince Vasin is here, Your Highness.

243
00:21:51,754 --> 00:21:52,755
Dad?

244
00:22:00,532 --> 00:22:02,382
Everything is under control,

245
00:22:04,222 --> 00:22:06,122
so I escorted Prince Vasin back safely.

246
00:22:07,022 --> 00:22:08,523
Thank you so much Phob,

247
00:22:08,780 --> 00:22:11,622
for taking care of my son.

248
00:22:14,156 --> 00:22:16,142
You don't need to thank him.

249
00:22:16,257 --> 00:22:17,258
Why's that?

250
00:22:17,322 --> 00:22:18,333
He's one of the rebels.

251
00:22:18,886 --> 00:22:19,887
What?

252
00:22:20,284 --> 00:22:21,285
Phob!

253
00:22:24,566 --> 00:22:25,567
You rebel!

254
00:22:25,742 --> 00:22:27,542
You think you can change anything?

255
00:22:28,062 --> 00:22:29,870
You can change the entire kingdom,

256
00:22:30,105 --> 00:22:32,705
but you'll never change the servant's
blood running through your veins.

257
00:22:32,729 --> 00:22:34,929
In the end, you'll always be
nothing more than lowborn.

258
00:22:38,782 --> 00:22:40,262
Noblemen like you are the very reason

259
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:44,102
the old regime had to fall.

260
00:22:45,678 --> 00:22:49,742
It upheld a system that
allowed those born into nobility

261
00:22:50,601 --> 00:22:52,222
to oppress others

262
00:22:52,942 --> 00:22:54,382
and take advantage of people

263
00:22:56,478 --> 00:22:58,262
regardless of their ability.

264
00:22:59,081 --> 00:23:02,134
They relied solely on the privilege of
their birth while bleeding the nation dry.

265
00:23:02,158 --> 00:23:03,182
- Phob!
- Phob!

266
00:23:07,492 --> 00:23:08,641
Let me ask you one thing.

267
00:23:09,222 --> 00:23:12,622
So, you truly think we're that cruel?

268
00:23:13,292 --> 00:23:16,262
That we've oppressed you so terribly?

269
00:23:20,417 --> 00:23:21,952
That's not what I meant.

270
00:23:25,516 --> 00:23:28,742
I've always been
grateful for your kindness.

271
00:23:30,684 --> 00:23:32,902
But we need changes in this country.

272
00:23:34,801 --> 00:23:35,802
Whatever.

273
00:23:36,678 --> 00:23:40,422
Be that as it may, I appreciate you

274
00:23:41,001 --> 00:23:43,262
bringing my son home.

275
00:23:43,881 --> 00:23:45,382
Vasin, let's go.

276
00:23:46,814 --> 00:23:50,022
We shouldn't take up any more of.

277
00:23:50,193 --> 00:23:52,782
Captain Phobthee's valuable time.

278
00:23:53,686 --> 00:23:54,687
Let's go, darling.

279
00:24:02,105 --> 00:24:03,106
Your Highness!

280
00:24:03,401 --> 00:24:04,402
- Your Highness!
- Stop!

281
00:24:05,993 --> 00:24:06,994
You need to leave now!

282
00:24:08,126 --> 00:24:09,127
Go!

283
00:24:10,132 --> 00:24:12,182
And don't ever set
foot in this palace again.

284
00:24:13,924 --> 00:24:15,422
I need to talk to Prince Tinnakorn.

285
00:24:15,801 --> 00:24:17,598
- Your Highness!
- My son wouldn't want to speak…

286
00:24:17,622 --> 00:24:19,017
to a traitor like you!

287
00:24:20,134 --> 00:24:21,135
Get out of here!

288
00:24:22,172 --> 00:24:25,542
Don't think for a second that I'm scared
of you just because you've got power.

289
00:24:27,062 --> 00:24:28,063
Go!

290
00:24:28,838 --> 00:24:29,839
- Your Highness!
- Go!

291
00:24:29,865 --> 00:24:32,742
Phob, we need to leave!
We don't want any trouble.

292
00:25:10,350 --> 00:25:11,351
Dad?

293
00:25:16,041 --> 00:25:17,042
Dad, I'm sorry.

294
00:25:20,436 --> 00:25:22,122
I was so stupid.

295
00:25:24,422 --> 00:25:26,202
It all happened because of me.

296
00:25:28,166 --> 00:25:29,167
I'm sorry.

297
00:25:34,657 --> 00:25:35,782
You did nothing wrong.

298
00:25:36,886 --> 00:25:38,982
It was all Phob's fault.

299
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:42,828
He hurt you, he hurt all of us,

300
00:25:44,161 --> 00:25:45,162
you understand?

301
00:25:48,940 --> 00:25:50,902
I won't let this end easily.

302
00:25:52,444 --> 00:25:54,582
They are the ones who will be defeated.

303
00:25:55,602 --> 00:25:58,862
They will pay for the evil
they've they have done to our nation.

304
00:26:03,143 --> 00:26:04,342
But it started because of me.

305
00:26:08,374 --> 00:26:09,375
I'm sorry.

306
00:26:28,854 --> 00:26:29,855
You should drink this.

307
00:26:46,212 --> 00:26:47,652
Don't think too much about it, Phob.

308
00:26:49,598 --> 00:26:52,582
If Prince Tinnakorn were to
hear your side of the story,

309
00:26:53,922 --> 00:26:56,062
he might understand you better.

310
00:27:11,462 --> 00:27:12,942
We succeeded in changing the country,

311
00:27:17,260 --> 00:27:18,742
yet I was left with no one.

312
00:27:26,580 --> 00:27:27,672
My mom is mad at me.

313
00:27:30,222 --> 00:27:31,382
Prince Tinnakorn…

314
00:27:35,566 --> 00:27:36,567
also left me.

315
00:27:42,958 --> 00:27:43,959
In the end...

316
00:27:46,876 --> 00:27:47,942
was the path I chose

317
00:27:51,489 --> 00:27:52,742
truly worth it?

318
00:28:00,321 --> 00:28:02,662
No one can answer that
in just a day or two, Phob.

319
00:28:04,392 --> 00:28:05,522
What we've done

320
00:28:06,833 --> 00:28:09,262
is far too great for people
to understand overnight.

321
00:28:11,542 --> 00:28:12,902
What should I do?

322
00:28:14,065 --> 00:28:15,066
Show the world

323
00:28:16,641 --> 00:28:18,542
that what we did was not in vain.

324
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:22,122
Show them that it truly
made our nation better.

325
00:28:23,382 --> 00:28:24,383
So that one day,

326
00:28:25,809 --> 00:28:29,302
everyone who suffered and everyone
who lost someone because of this

327
00:28:30,748 --> 00:28:33,122
will know their sacrifice
was not for nothing.

328
00:28:44,497 --> 00:28:45,582
I don't know

329
00:28:47,062 --> 00:28:48,742
how long it'll take.

330
00:28:50,004 --> 00:28:51,302
Right now, all I want…

331
00:28:52,964 --> 00:28:56,874
is to see and speak to him one more time.

332
00:29:08,844 --> 00:29:09,845
Phob,

333
00:29:11,694 --> 00:29:13,382
I can think of someone who can help you.

334
00:29:33,505 --> 00:29:34,506
Princess Ruethaisiri?

335
00:29:35,740 --> 00:29:38,782
Thank you for coming here to see me.

336
00:29:55,252 --> 00:29:57,982
Is it true that you're one of them?

337
00:29:59,865 --> 00:30:00,866
Yes,

338
00:30:01,572 --> 00:30:03,902
I am one of their supporters.

339
00:30:05,382 --> 00:30:07,142
Do you despise me for it?

340
00:30:13,169 --> 00:30:17,422
My father said that you
resented the nobility like us,

341
00:30:17,812 --> 00:30:19,502
and would lead the nation to ruin.

342
00:30:24,177 --> 00:30:26,662
Do you truly think I'm that kind of person?

343
00:30:29,729 --> 00:30:31,322
I don't know what to think.

344
00:30:33,510 --> 00:30:35,122
This change

345
00:30:36,372 --> 00:30:38,742
may have taken something away

346
00:30:39,369 --> 00:30:40,982
from noblewomen like you.

347
00:30:43,273 --> 00:30:44,522
But at the same time,

348
00:30:45,122 --> 00:30:48,742
it has given countless others
what they never had before.

349
00:30:50,373 --> 00:30:51,422
Really?

350
00:30:54,134 --> 00:30:56,062
Until now, Siam's future

351
00:30:56,382 --> 00:30:58,463
has been decided by
only a handful of people.

352
00:31:02,361 --> 00:31:04,522
But from this day forward,
whether rich or poor,

353
00:31:06,222 --> 00:31:08,942
every one of us will have
a say in our nation's future.

354
00:31:11,764 --> 00:31:13,322
Including me?

355
00:31:15,782 --> 00:31:18,342
That's right. You will have the freedom

356
00:31:19,529 --> 00:31:21,542
to choose what you want to do,

357
00:31:22,217 --> 00:31:23,622
to choose your own life,

358
00:31:24,489 --> 00:31:26,649
instead of living the life
others have chosen for you.

359
00:31:30,686 --> 00:31:33,862
Perhaps, my father was wrong.

360
00:31:46,532 --> 00:31:47,533
Actually,

361
00:31:48,686 --> 00:31:51,742
I asked to see you today

362
00:31:54,710 --> 00:31:57,462
because I have a favor to ask of you.

363
00:32:06,616 --> 00:32:09,022
Thank you for checking in on us.

364
00:32:10,510 --> 00:32:12,782
How is your father holding up?

365
00:32:14,004 --> 00:32:15,822
He is doing good, sir.

366
00:32:19,092 --> 00:32:22,022
Your Highness, Mr. Adul
is asking to see you.

367
00:32:53,404 --> 00:32:54,405
My beloved prince,

368
00:32:56,404 --> 00:32:57,742
I'm not sure

369
00:32:58,287 --> 00:33:01,262
whether you still wish to read this letter.

370
00:33:02,961 --> 00:33:04,622
Even so, I still wanted to write it,

371
00:33:06,689 --> 00:33:10,422
though I no longer have the
right to ask anything from you.

372
00:33:11,260 --> 00:33:14,262
I know what I did

373
00:33:15,701 --> 00:33:17,872
shattered your trust in me

374
00:33:18,641 --> 00:33:20,022
beyond forgiveness.

375
00:33:25,620 --> 00:33:26,942
There were times I wondered

376
00:33:29,599 --> 00:33:31,159
if everything could have been different

377
00:33:33,377 --> 00:33:36,202
had I chosen otherwise.

378
00:33:42,460 --> 00:33:43,982
But I had no choice.

379
00:33:46,412 --> 00:33:47,782
What I saw

380
00:33:50,545 --> 00:33:53,342
was never just about you and me.

381
00:33:54,700 --> 00:33:57,982
It was about countless people

382
00:33:58,590 --> 00:34:01,782
who were never given the
chance to choose their own lives.

383
00:34:03,182 --> 00:34:04,942
I wanted to see a world

384
00:34:06,361 --> 00:34:08,782
where no one would have to suffer simply

385
00:34:10,022 --> 00:34:11,782
because they were born
beneath someone else.

386
00:34:12,345 --> 00:34:13,942
And I still believe that

387
00:34:14,161 --> 00:34:16,322
when our country truly changes,

388
00:34:17,122 --> 00:34:20,822
when everyone is free
to choose their own path,

389
00:34:22,774 --> 00:34:24,422
our love will no longer

390
00:34:25,766 --> 00:34:28,422
have to remain a secret.

391
00:34:30,286 --> 00:34:33,287
I am not asking you to forgive me.

392
00:34:34,652 --> 00:34:35,882
I am not asking you

393
00:34:37,564 --> 00:34:39,502
to understand me right away.

394
00:34:43,020 --> 00:34:44,522
I just want

395
00:34:45,622 --> 00:34:47,623
you to know that.

396
00:34:50,198 --> 00:34:51,262
I've loved you

397
00:34:53,199 --> 00:34:54,200
every single day,

398
00:34:56,916 --> 00:34:58,522
and I always will.

399
00:35:37,148 --> 00:35:38,149
Your Highness.

400
00:35:39,149 --> 00:35:40,222
How is it?

401
00:35:42,433 --> 00:35:45,122
Did he agree to meet me?

402
00:35:55,788 --> 00:35:57,462
Tinnakorn asked me to give you this.

403
00:36:15,411 --> 00:36:19,262
On the day when the revolution started,

404
00:36:20,196 --> 00:36:21,822
his father followed him here

405
00:36:25,404 --> 00:36:27,823
and dragged him back to be
locked away in the palace.

406
00:36:28,726 --> 00:36:30,262
But Grandma and Aum

407
00:36:31,169 --> 00:36:32,702
helped him out of the palace.

408
00:36:40,638 --> 00:36:41,639
At first,

409
00:36:43,518 --> 00:36:45,662
he decided to run away with you.

410
00:36:47,566 --> 00:36:49,286
But before he even had a chance to see you,

411
00:36:50,422 --> 00:36:51,902
everything fell apart.

412
00:37:02,022 --> 00:37:03,023
He was willing

413
00:37:04,122 --> 00:37:05,162
to leave everything behind

414
00:37:06,313 --> 00:37:07,382
just to be with me.

415
00:37:09,294 --> 00:37:10,662
And how did I repay him?

416
00:37:17,017 --> 00:37:18,018
By betraying him.

417
00:37:48,579 --> 00:37:49,580
In the end,

418
00:37:55,204 --> 00:37:56,924
it turned out exactly as Prince Vasin said.

419
00:37:58,918 --> 00:38:01,222
I was never worthy of being with my prince.

420
00:38:28,116 --> 00:38:29,902
If my tree dies, I will be so mad at you.

421
00:38:30,558 --> 00:38:32,062
I am planting it neatly.

422
00:38:32,660 --> 00:38:33,780
You have to do a better job.

423
00:38:35,668 --> 00:38:38,190
Look at this spot, right here.

424
00:38:40,126 --> 00:38:41,382
And that spot, right there.

425
00:38:43,486 --> 00:38:45,742
Come on, you have to
work harder, Mr. Phobthee.

426
00:38:47,364 --> 00:38:49,862
- Work harder? Really?
- Phob!

427
00:38:49,953 --> 00:38:51,147
Let me go!

428
00:38:52,662 --> 00:38:55,022
You are using me, you
let me do all the work.

429
00:38:55,878 --> 00:38:56,879
Are you going to help me?

430
00:38:58,294 --> 00:39:01,142
You stink so bad, let me go!

431
00:39:01,361 --> 00:39:03,842
- Do I stink?
- That's right.

432
00:39:03,905 --> 00:39:06,462
- Do I stink?
- Yeah, you stink!

433
00:39:06,806 --> 00:39:07,807
You said I stink?

434
00:39:24,550 --> 00:39:25,670
Didn't you just say I stink?

435
00:39:45,622 --> 00:39:47,022
Phob, I'm so happy.

436
00:39:50,566 --> 00:39:52,867
I want us to stay
together like this forever.

437
00:40:02,422 --> 00:40:03,423
Sure, we can.

438
00:40:05,122 --> 00:40:06,622
If you won't let go of my hand,

439
00:40:07,705 --> 00:40:09,706
I won't let go of yours.

440
00:40:16,022 --> 00:40:17,142
That is not going to happen.

441
00:41:18,001 --> 00:41:20,722
Judging by the list of the
70 provisional representatives,

442
00:41:21,142 --> 00:41:22,719
there are roughly equal numbers
from the Khana Ratsadon

443
00:41:22,743 --> 00:41:25,542
and senior officials of the old regime.

444
00:41:26,062 --> 00:41:28,622
I believe it's meant to demonstrate
a willingness to compromise.

445
00:41:30,084 --> 00:41:31,518
Others may surrender if they want.

446
00:41:32,116 --> 00:41:35,782
But we're not going down without a fight.
We have to find a way to get rid of them.

447
00:41:38,660 --> 00:41:39,661
Get them in the car.

448
00:41:40,404 --> 00:41:43,102
What's this? Where are you going?

449
00:41:48,953 --> 00:41:49,954
What did you say?

450
00:41:50,436 --> 00:41:54,582
Prince Noppalak was even
forced into exile overseas?

451
00:41:57,486 --> 00:41:58,822
It's not just one palace.

452
00:41:59,913 --> 00:42:03,169
Many members of the royal family are
now concerned for their safety.

453
00:42:04,054 --> 00:42:06,542
Some are preparing to
go into exile in Penang,

454
00:42:07,660 --> 00:42:10,422
while others are planning to leave
for Bandung on Java Island.

455
00:42:12,406 --> 00:42:14,862
Siam is truly entering a dark age.

456
00:42:16,297 --> 00:42:20,446
Will our family be safe after this?

457
00:42:21,838 --> 00:42:23,662
I'm starting to get scared.

458
00:42:23,865 --> 00:42:26,302
I don't think we should panic just yet.

459
00:42:28,228 --> 00:42:32,622
Most of the royals being targeted
by the Khana Ratsadon

460
00:42:33,174 --> 00:42:35,654
are those in high-ranking positions
who refused to compromise.

461
00:42:36,385 --> 00:42:39,342
Several others have expressed support

462
00:42:39,756 --> 00:42:42,262
for the change in government,

463
00:42:42,742 --> 00:42:44,422
and it looks like

464
00:42:44,489 --> 00:42:46,881
they'll be appointed to key positions
in the new government.

465
00:42:46,905 --> 00:42:49,182
Cowards. Self-serving cowards.

466
00:42:49,956 --> 00:42:51,622
What a disgrace to the royal family.

467
00:42:53,033 --> 00:42:54,542
Everything's in chaos.

468
00:43:01,286 --> 00:43:03,862
We haven't been able
to go to work for days.

469
00:43:04,187 --> 00:43:06,388
I can't even get into the ministry.

470
00:43:06,689 --> 00:43:08,662
Why are you so hardworking these days?

471
00:43:11,004 --> 00:43:12,662
I need to take care of something at work.

472
00:43:15,889 --> 00:43:21,039
The People's Committee of Siam is responsible
for carrying out the Assembly's resolutions.

473
00:43:21,064 --> 00:43:26,222
It oversees government administration,
including directing government officials,

474
00:43:26,247 --> 00:43:30,123
recommending appointments
and dismissals, and submitting matters to

475
00:43:30,147 --> 00:43:35,035
His Majesty King Prajadhipok for royal
signature and guidance on affairs of state.

476
00:43:35,588 --> 00:43:37,622
Are they going to dismiss
government officials?

477
00:43:53,118 --> 00:43:55,222
Can't we get our money back first?

478
00:43:55,494 --> 00:43:57,022
I'm worried they'll investigate.

479
00:43:57,414 --> 00:44:00,822
If they find out I invested the
ministry's money with you, I'm finished.

480
00:44:01,084 --> 00:44:02,116
Your Highness,

481
00:44:02,416 --> 00:44:06,798
can't you see how
dangerous things have become?

482
00:44:09,137 --> 00:44:10,138
Come on.

483
00:44:10,828 --> 00:44:13,582
I don't think our luck is that bad.

484
00:44:25,363 --> 00:44:27,945
What? Are you going to shut
down some of newspapers?

485
00:44:31,716 --> 00:44:33,182
I don't like doing this either.

486
00:44:35,340 --> 00:44:39,142
But supporters of the old regime attack us
through the newspapers every day.

487
00:44:40,998 --> 00:44:42,782
Some even claim we're an oligarchy

488
00:44:43,249 --> 00:44:44,922
that only serves its own interests.

489
00:44:46,742 --> 00:44:49,782
But if we do this, we're
destroying freedom.

490
00:44:50,382 --> 00:44:51,902
Before the change in government,

491
00:44:52,308 --> 00:44:54,822
every side debated through the newspapers.

492
00:44:56,625 --> 00:44:57,626
If we do this,

493
00:44:58,716 --> 00:45:00,772
can we really call it democracy?

494
00:45:02,220 --> 00:45:03,822
Let's just get through this first.

495
00:45:05,078 --> 00:45:06,822
Once everything settles down,

496
00:45:07,326 --> 00:45:10,422
I promise I'll speak to those in charge
and make them understand.

497
00:45:11,060 --> 00:45:13,182
We fought for democracy.

498
00:45:13,822 --> 00:45:17,423
I know freedom is one of
the most important values in this country.

499
00:45:23,105 --> 00:45:25,082
Phob, what do you think?

500
00:45:30,140 --> 00:45:32,942
I don't think it'll do any
harm if it's only temporary.

501
00:45:35,141 --> 00:45:37,722
Right now, the country needs unity.

502
00:45:40,377 --> 00:45:41,772
Phob is right.

503
00:45:43,006 --> 00:45:45,144
The Assembly's work

504
00:45:45,876 --> 00:45:49,072
and the drafting of the
constitution are proceeding smoothly.

505
00:45:49,934 --> 00:45:52,582
Even members of the royal
family have been very cooperative.

506
00:45:53,422 --> 00:45:54,502
Except one thing.

507
00:46:03,628 --> 00:46:06,782
These government officials are
to be dismissed immediately,

508
00:46:07,505 --> 00:46:10,806
as they may pose a threat to democracy.

509
00:46:26,382 --> 00:46:28,924
[M.C. Chatthorn Varakulvatin]
[M.C. Tinnakorn Varakulvatin]

510
00:46:36,662 --> 00:46:37,863
[M.C. Tinnakorn Varakulvatin]

511
00:46:43,924 --> 00:46:44,925
Really?

512
00:46:45,577 --> 00:46:48,382
Are all of you being forced
to leave the ministries?

513
00:46:53,401 --> 00:46:55,342
Prince Chatthorn, please stay calm.

514
00:46:57,166 --> 00:46:59,382
They are trying to nip
any opposition in the bud.

515
00:46:59,918 --> 00:47:01,641
The royals and government officials

516
00:47:01,790 --> 00:47:04,569
who came up under the old regime
and refused to submit to them

517
00:47:04,708 --> 00:47:05,909
have all been dismissed.

518
00:47:08,185 --> 00:47:09,186
And it's not just us.

519
00:47:10,026 --> 00:47:13,742
The heads of the Provincial
Police, the Opium Department,

520
00:47:14,201 --> 00:47:17,462
the Lands Department, and the Marine
Department have all been dismissed.

521
00:47:19,422 --> 00:47:22,223
Dad… what are we going to do after this?

522
00:47:23,187 --> 00:47:24,222
What should we do?

523
00:47:25,321 --> 00:47:27,702
Don't you worry about your work.

524
00:47:27,966 --> 00:47:31,500
The ministry is a big
organization. Even without you,

525
00:47:31,622 --> 00:47:33,622
they'll find someone else to do the job.

526
00:47:33,985 --> 00:47:35,238
Right now,

527
00:47:35,761 --> 00:47:40,382
we should be more concerned
about our own lives and our safety.

528
00:47:40,722 --> 00:47:41,723
Okay, Grandma.

529
00:48:47,249 --> 00:48:48,250
Dad?

530
00:48:53,257 --> 00:48:54,258
Dad,

531
00:48:55,268 --> 00:48:56,269
I'm sorry.

532
00:48:57,006 --> 00:48:59,422
It's my fault everyone's suffering.

533
00:48:59,462 --> 00:49:01,202
I caused all of this.

534
00:49:03,569 --> 00:49:05,542
I told you, none of this is your fault.

535
00:49:08,322 --> 00:49:11,122
It's the traitors who betrayed our nation.

536
00:49:17,622 --> 00:49:19,262
But I'll never surrender to them.

537
00:49:21,345 --> 00:49:23,622
I won't let them destroy our Siam.

538
00:49:33,164 --> 00:49:34,165
Sir?

539
00:49:39,147 --> 00:49:41,627
I respectfully disagree
with your decision to dismiss everyone

540
00:49:42,475 --> 00:49:43,582
from the Varakulvatin.

541
00:49:45,209 --> 00:49:48,742
Prince Vasin is the driving force
behind the Blue Ribbon faction.

542
00:49:49,438 --> 00:49:52,782
The senior authorities believe that
this group is intent on destroying us.

543
00:49:53,470 --> 00:49:54,471
Therefore,

544
00:49:55,246 --> 00:49:58,422
everyone from the Varakulvatin
must be removed from government service,

545
00:49:58,964 --> 00:50:00,662
including Prince Tinnakorn.

546
00:50:01,433 --> 00:50:04,134
Prince Tinnakorn has nothing to do
with the Blue Ribbon faction.

547
00:50:04,964 --> 00:50:06,462
I'd stake my life on it.

548
00:50:07,310 --> 00:50:11,142
If any of the senior
authorities refuse to believe me,

549
00:50:15,356 --> 00:50:16,596
I'll meet with them personally.

550
00:50:17,494 --> 00:50:19,782
I know you're close to Prince Tinnakorn,

551
00:50:20,849 --> 00:50:24,289
but don't let your personal feelings stand
in the way of the country's transformation.

552
00:50:27,169 --> 00:50:30,453
I've used my personal
relationship with Prince Tinnakorn,

553
00:50:31,516 --> 00:50:33,702
and the trust he placed in me,

554
00:50:34,777 --> 00:50:35,902
to carry out our mission.

555
00:50:37,804 --> 00:50:39,305
You should trust my judgment.

556
00:50:40,617 --> 00:50:43,886
Prince Tinnakorn would never betray us.

557
00:50:43,966 --> 00:50:45,998
We've come this far. We can't afford
to make any mistakes now, Phob.

558
00:50:46,022 --> 00:50:47,023
I know that.

559
00:50:49,100 --> 00:50:51,820
You can have me watch Prince Tinnakorn
around the clock if you wish.

560
00:50:52,950 --> 00:50:54,222
But I ask just one thing,

561
00:50:55,441 --> 00:50:57,401
please don't dismiss him
from government service.

562
00:51:04,516 --> 00:51:05,517
Sir,

563
00:51:06,958 --> 00:51:08,518
I've risked my life for this revolution

564
00:51:10,950 --> 00:51:12,622
just as everyone else has.

565
00:51:14,502 --> 00:51:17,982
I've never asked for a government position
or any reward.

566
00:51:21,734 --> 00:51:22,902
This is the only request.

567
00:51:24,529 --> 00:51:25,622
I've ever made of you.

568
00:51:30,204 --> 00:51:31,205
Phob, I am so sorry.

569
00:51:34,908 --> 00:51:36,822
This isn't my decision alone.

570
00:51:39,420 --> 00:51:40,620
The senior authorities believe

571
00:51:42,033 --> 00:51:43,825
this is the best course of action.

572
00:52:14,142 --> 00:52:16,612
Why? Why does it have to be you?

573
00:52:17,689 --> 00:52:19,302
Ever since I started working here,

574
00:52:19,566 --> 00:52:21,867
I've never met anyone
more hardworking than you.

575
00:52:22,689 --> 00:52:24,142
Even though you're a prince,

576
00:52:25,238 --> 00:52:29,982
you never once left the work to low-ranking
officials like me, even though you could've.

577
00:52:35,836 --> 00:52:37,182
Just think of it as fate

578
00:52:38,342 --> 00:52:40,142
playing a cruel joke on me.

579
00:53:02,465 --> 00:53:03,467
Your Highness.

580
00:53:06,782 --> 00:53:08,462
Mr. Phobthee, what can I do for you, sir?

581
00:53:13,620 --> 00:53:14,662
I will help you

582
00:53:15,945 --> 00:53:16,946
with your job.

583
00:53:17,976 --> 00:53:20,977
I swear I will have you reinstated.

584
00:53:22,260 --> 00:53:24,822
I'll speak to the senior authorities
myself. I give you my word.

585
00:53:25,102 --> 00:53:26,182
There's no need.

586
00:53:29,341 --> 00:53:31,262
I'm no longer of any use to you.

587
00:53:33,662 --> 00:53:35,782
You don't have to go
through all that trouble for me.

588
00:53:42,433 --> 00:53:43,434
Your Highness.

589
00:53:45,242 --> 00:53:46,722
Please, Your Highness, don't do this.

590
00:53:48,582 --> 00:53:49,622
I know I've done wrong.

591
00:53:51,505 --> 00:53:53,982
I was at fault, and I'm truly sorry.

592
00:53:56,985 --> 00:53:58,742
But the love I have for you,

593
00:54:01,097 --> 00:54:02,522
it is real.

594
00:54:04,865 --> 00:54:05,866
Phob,

595
00:54:07,169 --> 00:54:08,502
if you could turn back time,

596
00:54:10,705 --> 00:54:11,982
would you do the same?

597
00:54:24,441 --> 00:54:25,442
I would.

598
00:54:33,886 --> 00:54:34,942
The change in the system

599
00:54:36,820 --> 00:54:38,420
was bound to happen, one way or another.

600
00:54:40,100 --> 00:54:41,782
But there's one thing I would never do,

601
00:54:43,028 --> 00:54:45,322
I would never drag you into this plan.

602
00:54:47,508 --> 00:54:49,722
I would never let you get hurt like this.

603
00:55:00,272 --> 00:55:01,273
I understand.

604
00:55:03,540 --> 00:55:05,062
I appreciate your honesty.

605
00:55:07,647 --> 00:55:08,648
I believe you.

606
00:55:15,601 --> 00:55:16,922
If you believe me,

607
00:55:19,662 --> 00:55:21,022
can we go back to normal?

608
00:55:22,463 --> 00:55:23,742
Please, don't leave me. Please?

609
00:55:25,164 --> 00:55:26,165
Phob.

610
00:55:28,444 --> 00:55:30,502
Phob, I understand your intentions.

611
00:55:31,617 --> 00:55:33,532
I understand what you stand for.

612
00:55:35,649 --> 00:55:38,222
And I truly believe that you want
what's best for this country.

613
00:55:41,420 --> 00:55:42,421
But…

614
00:55:43,857 --> 00:55:45,822
we are two people who can't be in love.

615
00:55:47,793 --> 00:55:48,794
No!

616
00:55:49,502 --> 00:55:50,503
No! No!

617
00:55:51,332 --> 00:55:52,542
Please, don't be like this.

618
00:55:53,513 --> 00:55:55,022
I truly love you.

619
00:55:57,673 --> 00:55:58,674
Let me go.

620
00:56:07,694 --> 00:56:08,702
Goodbye.

621
00:56:11,305 --> 00:56:12,306
I wish you all the best.

622
00:57:21,200 --> 00:57:25,200
(Next Episode) I don't want to be an obstacle
that forces you to choose between me...

623
00:57:26,200 --> 00:57:27,800
and what you believe in.

624
00:57:28,000 --> 00:57:30,000
I will watch your success from afar.

625
00:57:37,400 --> 00:57:40,900
Lord Chatthorn, Your Highness is being
charged with embezzlement...

626
00:57:42,900 --> 00:57:46,400
Given only two weeks,
there is no way to gather that much money!
